        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Jacksonville Jaguars, National Football League, University of Southern California Trojans\n- People: Jack Del Rio, Mel Tucker\n- Roles: head coach, defensive coordinator, linebacker\n- Events: 2011 Jacksonville Jaguars season, Jack Del Rio's firing and interim replacement\n\nFacts:\n- Jack Del Rio played as a linebacker for four NFL teams between 1985 and 1996.\n- Jack Del Rio played both football and baseball for the University of Southern California Trojans.\n- The 2011 Jacksonville Jaguars season was the franchise's 17th season in the National Football League.\n- The 2011 Jacksonville Jaguars season was the team's 9th season under head coach Jack Del Rio.\n- On November 29, 2011, the Jacksonville Jaguars fired head coach Jack Del Rio.\n- After Jack Del Rio was fired, the Jacksonville Jaguars replaced him on an interim basis with defensive coordinator Mel Tucker.",
